我们没有消除这种猜测，也没有证实或否认。

00:27:29.589 --> 00:27:38.089
We made people wait two weeks back when these episodes used to be every Monday and not all at once to figure out who she was.
当这些剧集过去每周一播出而不是一次性放出时，我们让大家等了两个星期才弄清楚她是谁。

00:27:38.089 --> 00:27:45.410
What's your memory of you get thrown into this one of Ted's greatest rom-com outings, I think, right?
你对被卷入泰德最棒的浪漫喜剧出场之一有什么记忆吗？我觉得是这样的，对吧？

00:27:45.410 --> 00:27:51.890
The wedding plus drum roll that hour is one of the best Ted romantic comedy, kind of its own mini little movie.
婚礼加上《鼓声》（Drumroll）那一小时是泰德最好的浪漫喜剧之一，有点像它自己的微型小电影。

00:27:51.890 --> 00:27:52.890
How did you feel?
你当时感觉怎么样？

00:27:52.890 --> 00:27:53.890
How did you announce that?
你是怎么宣布这一点的？

00:27:53.890 --> 00:27:54.890
Can you ask you a little bit, right?
能问你一点吗，对吧？

00:27:54.890 --> 00:28:00.529
you guys connect, how did you feel working with her like this, like in this very intense way at all of a sudden?
你们很合拍，突然之间以这种非常强烈的方式和她合作，你感觉怎么样？

00:28:00.529 --> 00:28:09.930
I think the charm and the ease one feels watching her as Victoria, you know, the kind of open.
我觉得看着她饰演维多利亚时，人们会感受到一种迷人和轻松，你知道那种开放的感觉。

00:28:09.930 --> 00:28:20.200
There's like a silliness to her, like in the best kind of way, like a kind of like she can be both sincere and such a goofball, which is so charming.
她身上有一种傻乎乎的特质，是以最好的一种方式，既能真诚又能当个十足的活宝，这太迷人了。

00:28:20.200 --> 00:28:25.779
And I think, I don't know, I immediately felt like this allyship with her.
而且我觉得，我不知道，我立刻就对她产生了一种同盟感。

00:28:25.779 --> 00:28:36.000
I felt like, oh, this is a great addition to the cast for this story we're telling, and also just like a really great person to be in the trenches with.
我觉得，哦，对于我们正在讲的故事来说，这是演员阵容中极好的一员，而且也是一个非常适合并肩作战的好伙伴。

00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:41.380
I mean, she had done a lot of stuff and she knew the drill.
我的意思是，她演过很多作品，她懂这一行。

00:28:41.380 --> 00:28:46.680
I think sitcom acting is deceptively hard.
我认为情景喜剧表演有着欺骗性的难度。

00:28:46.680 --> 00:28:47.680
Yeah.
对。

00:28:47.680 --> 00:28:49.880
I think the best ones make it look quite easy.
我觉得最棒的演员能把它演得看起来很简单。

00:28:49.880 --> 00:28:54.720
It's like, that's part of the trick of it, is that it looks kind of easy.
这就像是其中的诀窍之一，就是它看起来挺容易的。

00:28:54.720 --> 00:29:04.480
But I remember feeling, especially in drum roll, like I remember reading drum roll and being like, oh yeah, this is a good one for Ted, yeah.
但我记得当时的感觉，尤其是在拍《鼓声》的时候，我记得读《鼓声》的剧本时就在想，“哦，是的，这对泰德来说是个好故事，是的。”

00:29:04.480 --> 00:29:05.839
This is really good.
这真的很棒。

00:29:05.839 --> 00:29:10.680
And I liked getting to be heroic romantically.
而且我很喜欢在浪漫方面表现得很英勇。

00:29:10.680 --> 00:29:27.240
I thought like, if I'm asked to do one big thing in this show, it's to be like a romantic hero, like via hero for open-hearted, sincere, vulnerable dudes everywhere who really wanna meet someone and go for it, you know?
我觉得，如果在这部剧里让我做一件大事，那就是做一个浪漫的英雄，为天下所有心胸坦荡、真诚、脆弱、真正想遇到某人并勇往直前的男人们当英雄，你知道吗？

00:29:27.240 --> 00:29:36.160
And I think it was an untapped market like by the evidence of many men and women saying I relate to Ted so much, you know?
我觉得这是一个未被开发的市场，从许多男人和女人说“我和泰德太有共鸣了”就能看出这一点，你知道吗？

00:29:36.160 --> 00:29:54.799
So I think you guys really hit on an archetype that had been kind of unexplored because I think the idea was in culture like most men are like Barney, like they just, you know, the, you know, the old ball and chain, I don't want to be, you know, I'd rather be out with the boys or I'd rather be, you know, meeting someone.
所以我觉得你们确实触及了一种在文化中一直未被怎么探讨的原型，因为我觉得当时的文化观念是，大多数男人就像巴尼那样，你知道的，你知道那种“家有贤妻（老绊脚石）”的心态，我才不要，你知道的，我宁愿跟哥们儿出去，或者我宁愿去……你知道的，去认识别人。

00:29:54.799 --> 00:30:07.039
And I think you guys just wrote this guy that I helped bring to life with you that was a different breed, but really way more common than we realized.
而我觉得你们塑造了这个角色——我和你们一起把它带到了生活中——他是一个不同品种的男人，但实际上比我们意识到的要常见得多。

00:30:07.039 --> 00:30:23.210
And I also remember as the scenes wore on, like I remember like when the bow tie kind of came untied like I felt really like I was both as a character like really dropped into the moment very relaxed in a kind of like young Richard Gere.
我还记得随着场景的推进，就像我记得当领结解开的时候，我真的感觉自己既作为角色完全沉浸在当下，又非常放松，有点像年轻时的理查·基尔。

00:30:23.210 --> 00:30:32.353
You know, like it just felt like easy and Ashley has that thing of like if she's supposed to be attracted to you, you feel attractive.
你知道的，就感觉一切都很轻松，而阿什莉身上有一种特质：如果她本该被你吸引，你就会觉得自己很有吸引力。

00:30:32.353 --> 00:30:33.786
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:30:33.786 --> 00:30:39.244
Like she's got that like generous quality as an actress where she's helping you.
她作为演员有一种慷慨的品质，她在帮衬着你。

00:30:39.244 --> 00:30:41.701
You know, she's really playing long.
你知道的，她真的很配合。

00:30:41.701 --> 00:30:48.865
She laughs at your jokes in just the right way that makes you feel like, you know what, I'm pretty funny.
她恰到好处地对你的笑话笑出声来，让你觉得，你知道吗，我其实挺搞笑的。

00:30:48.865 --> 00:30:55.620
You know, and you're like, I don't know if that's Victoria or Ashley, but it's making me feel good.
你知道，你会想，我不知道这是维多利亚还是阿什莉，但这让我感觉很好。

00:30:55.620 --> 00:30:56.779
So yeah, totally.
所以，是的，完全如此。

00:30:56.779 --> 00:31:01.260
Yeah, I thought she was, I mean, I couldn't imagine anyone else playing the role.
对，我觉得她，我的意思是，我无法想象其他人来演这个角色。

00:31:01.260 --> 00:31:02.588
She's she was fantastic.
她太棒了。

00:31:02.588 --> 00:31:05.299
And she was always just a delight to have on set.
而且她在片场总是让人感到非常开心。

00:31:05.299 --> 00:31:10.056
She was always, she's one of those actors that always look like delighted to be there.
她总是，她是那种看起来总是很高兴能来到这里的演员。

00:31:10.056 --> 00:31:12.379
You know, She has that twinkle in her eye.
你知道，她眼里有光。

00:31:12.380 --> 00:31:13.339
She just has that thing.
她身上就是有那种特质。

00:31:13.339 --> 00:31:14.619
It's just like a little bit magic.
这就像是带有一点魔力。

00:31:14.619 --> 00:31:17.140
It kind of can't be faked or learned or practiced.
这种特质是无法伪造、学习或练习出来的。

00:31:17.140 --> 00:31:17.980
She has that thing.
她身上就有那种东西。

00:31:17.980 --> 00:31:25.220
And also, just a shout out, like she's been shown up for these Paul Grossfield events for years, you know, to help us raise money.
还有，顺便提一句，多年来她一直出席保罗·格罗斯菲尔德（Paul Grossfield）的这些活动，你知道的，来帮我们筹集资金。

00:31:25.220 --> 00:31:26.059
Yeah, I know.
对，我知道。

00:31:26.059 --> 00:31:27.380
I wanted to point that out too.
我也想指出这一点。

00:31:27.380 --> 00:31:33.900
All these years later, we do these, our band, the solids, we did the How Much Mother theme song and like Carter and I, it's a card on my band.
多年后的今天，我们还在做这些，我们的乐队The Solids，我们创作了《老爸老妈的浪漫史》的主题曲，我和卡特，那是卡特和我的乐队。

00:31:33.900 --> 00:31:36.619
And we wrote a lot of the silly song, How Much Mother.
我们写了这首傻乎乎的歌《老爸老妈的浪漫史》。

00:31:36.619 --> 00:31:41.869
And we do a charity fundraiser concert every year, past few years, we're going to keep doing it.
过去几年里，我们每年都举办一次慈善募捐音乐会，我们还会继续办下去。

00:31:41.869 --> 00:31:43.947
I will very much plug it on this show.
我非常乐意在这档节目里为它做宣传。

00:31:43.947 --> 00:31:46.134
It'll be some months away, the next one.
距离下一场还有好几个月。

00:31:46.134 --> 00:31:48.923
But Ashley always comes out and does the song list.
但阿什莉总是会来献唱。

00:31:48.923 --> 00:31:52.915
We did Victoria by the Kinks, which we use later in the series, spoilers.
我们唱了The Kinks的《Victoria》，我们在剧集后期也用了这首歌，剧透预警。

00:31:52.915 --> 00:31:55.376
Ashley, you can tell by how much we love her.
阿什莉，从我们有多爱她就能看出来。

00:31:55.376 --> 00:31:59.094
She comes back later if you're watching the show for the first time.
如果你是第一次看这部剧，你会发现她后来又回归了。

00:31:59.094 --> 00:32:03.195
Sorry, but I'm not sorry because you get more Ashley and so you're welcome.
很抱歉，但我一点也不觉得抱歉，因为你能看到更多阿什莉，所以不用谢。

00:32:03.195 --> 00:32:24.303
And so she comes out and she just she has such pride for having been part of how much her mother and she's such an open-hearted, amazing person that she loves to help raise money for this good cause, that the cause is to do research into congenital heart conditions for pediatric, you know, basically kids like my son who had open heart surgery, had any kind of congenital heart defect.
所以她来了，她为自己曾参演《老爸老妈的浪漫史》感到无比骄傲，她是一个如此心胸宽广、了不起的人，她喜欢为这个美好的原因筹集资金，这个原因就是研究小儿先天性心脏病，你知道的，基本上就是像我儿子那样做过心脏手术、患有任何先天性心脏缺陷的孩子。

00:32:24.303 --> 00:32:26.709
This is raising money to research into that.
这是在为相关的研究筹集资金。

00:32:26.709 --> 00:32:31.576
And she just like, she shows up, she flies from LA to New York to be part of the concert.
她就这样出席了，她从洛杉矶飞到纽约来参加这场音乐会。

00:32:31.576 --> 00:32:33.544
Josh has done every one of them too.
乔什也参加了每一次活动。

00:32:33.544 --> 00:32:34.419
Thank you, Josh.
谢谢你，乔什。

00:32:34.419 --> 00:32:36.060
And she's one of those people.
她就是那种人。

00:32:36.059 --> 00:32:37.788
she's just one of those people.
她真的是那种人。

00:32:37.788 --> 00:32:47.660
Going back to the scene of you guys playing at the piano, I was just going to say when we're talking about your chemistry, I loved the moment because she is so confident, right?
回到你们在钢琴前弹奏的那场戏，我正想说，当我们谈到你们的化学反应时，我非常喜欢那个时刻，因为她太自信了，对吧？

00:32:47.660 --> 00:32:49.724
She is the ringmaster of this, right?
她才是这个局的掌控者，对吧？

00:32:49.724 --> 00:33:05.340
She's laid down the rules of this game, we're not going to kiss, we're only going to drum roll, we're not going to tell each other any more information than these first names, which only reluctantly got spilled because of Barney and he's saying Ted 5,000 times, which is so funny.
她定下了这场游戏的规则：我们不接吻，我们只打鼓（指摇滚手势/暗号），我们除了名字之外不会向对方透露任何更多信息，而名字也只是因为巴尼一直在不停地喊“泰德”整整五千遍才勉强说漏嘴的，这太搞笑了。

00:33:05.339 --> 00:33:08.059
And also his insistence on saying it over and over.
还有他坚持不懈地一遍又一遍地喊。

00:33:08.059 --> 00:33:09.900
Ted, Ted.
泰德，泰德。

00:33:09.900 --> 00:33:11.220
So funny.
太搞笑了。

00:33:13.220 --> 00:33:22.299
But then there's this moment, the first time you guys almost kissed at that piano, which also it's funny because all of a sudden Ted's great at piano, I don't know if we ever showed Ted being ready to go back to that.
但随后有了这样一个时刻，你们第一次差点在钢琴旁接吻，这也很有趣，因为泰德突然变得擅长弹钢琴了，我不知道我们是否展示过泰德会弹琴这事儿。

00:33:22.299 --> 00:33:24.579
Yeah, it was a lot of weird little buys in there.
对，里面有很多奇怪的小巧思。

00:33:24.579 --> 00:33:37.460
But that moment where you guys almost kiss and she kind of pulls away, pulls back from fully kissing, And she looks so at that for just one moment, very helpless, very like she's under Ted's thrall there for a minute.
但就在你们几乎要接吻的那一刻，她有点退缩了，没有真正亲下去，仅仅那么一瞬间，她看起来是那么无助，就像是在那一分钟里完全被泰德迷住了。

00:33:37.460 --> 00:33:40.180
She's gone a little bit past where she meant to go.
她有点超出她原本的计划了。

00:33:40.180 --> 00:33:41.700
And she plays it in this great moment.
她在那个精彩的时刻把这个演得太棒了。

00:33:41.700 --> 00:33:45.859
And you realize she's been playing the whole thing so in control up to that moment.
你会发现，直到那一刻之前，她整场戏都掌控得游刃有余。

00:33:45.859 --> 00:33:49.099
And then she flips it in that moment.
然后就在那一刻，她来了个大反转。

00:33:49.099 --> 00:33:50.779
She shows that she's also vulnerable.
她展露了自己脆弱的一面。

00:33:50.779 --> 00:33:52.099
She's not running the signal.
她不是在发信号。

00:33:52.099 --> 00:33:54.220
So that was totally the signal.
所以那绝对就是信号。

00:33:54.220 --> 00:33:55.299
That was the signal.
那就是信号。

00:33:55.299 --> 00:33:57.259
I love how she played that moment.
我太喜欢她处理那个时刻的方式了。

00:33:57.259 --> 00:33:58.220
That is like a great acting.
这简直就是神级演技。

00:33:58.220 --> 00:34:02.900
I also love, it's kind of like that great thing of like use what's in the room, right?
我也很喜欢，这有点像那种绝佳的技巧：利用房间里现有的东西，对吧？

00:34:02.900 --> 00:34:07.660
He's on the piano, but when she says something about not kissing him, he hits all the bass notes.
他在弹钢琴，但当她说起没有吻他的事时，他用力弹了所有的低音。

00:34:07.660 --> 00:34:09.099
Yeah, oh my God, that was so funny.
对，哦天哪，太搞笑了。

00:34:09.099 --> 00:34:10.380
Yeah, that was such a great moment.
对，那真是个极好的时刻。

00:34:10.380 --> 00:34:13.460
Yeah, that was a laugh out loud from my wife Rebecca watching now.
对，我妻子丽贝卡（Rebecca）在看的时候直接笑出声了。

00:34:13.460 --> 00:34:16.500
Rebecca loves this two part or two, and I think it was like, this is a good dead one.
丽贝卡很喜欢这上下两集，我觉得当时她就觉得，这集真棒。

00:34:16.500 --> 00:34:18.579
You guys are gonna have fun talking about this one.
你们俩聊这一集肯定会聊得很开心。

00:34:18.579 --> 00:34:23.260
She laughed out loud at the minor chord in moment there.
她为刚才那个小调和弦的时刻大声笑了出来。

00:34:23.260 --> 00:34:24.099
So good.
太棒了。

00:34:24.099 --> 00:34:39.519
Alec, let's play Jordana's, this is of course, It's a section where we're calling, questions and observations from a clinical psychologist who's never seen how I met your mother and also happens to be married to Josh.
亚历克，我们来听听乔丹娜（Jordana）的留言，这当然是这样一个环节：我们邀请了一位临床心理学家的提问和观察，她从未看过《老爸老妈浪漫史》，而且恰好是乔什的妻子。

00:34:39.519 --> 00:34:44.920
I felt like this episode was some sort of turning point in the show for me.
我觉得对这部剧来说，这一集对我而言算是一个某种转折点。

00:34:44.920 --> 00:34:50.400
Halfway through I said to Josh, I'm suddenly feeling very attached to these characters.
看到一半的时候，我对乔什说，我突然开始对这些角色产生强烈的羁绊了。

00:34:50.400 --> 00:34:55.920
I was laughing harder at the jokes, certain moments were tugging at the heartstrings more deeply.
我对笑话的反应更强烈了，某些时刻也更能触动心弦。

00:34:55.920 --> 00:34:59.400
But later I was reflecting on why that might be.
但后来我一直在反思这是为什么。

00:34:59.400 --> 00:35:05.440
And I think for me, it's because it's the first episode where Robin showed real vulnerability.
我想对我来说，是因为这是罗宾展现出真实脆弱感的第一集。

00:35:05.440 --> 00:35:12.840
It's almost like I couldn't be fully in, I couldn't fully fall for this love story until she did.
就好像在这一刻到来之前，我无法全身心投入，无法真正爱上这个爱情故事。

00:35:12.840 --> 00:35:15.159
This is the first time we see her cry.
这是我们第一次看到她哭。

00:35:15.159 --> 00:35:19.679
We see that she really feels what Ted is feeling too.
我们看到她也真正感受到了泰德的感受。

00:35:19.679 --> 00:35:39.119
And the title Drumroll, please, which we think is about the anticipation between Victoria and Ted, I actually think on a deeper level is about Ted and Robin, and their long, drawn out drumroll and the audience staying in that anticipation with them for many, many years.
而剧名《鼓声响起，请》，我们原本以为是指维多利亚和泰德之间的悬念，但实际上，我觉得在更深的层面上，它是指泰德和罗宾，指他们漫长而拖沓的“鼓声”，以及观众陪伴他们多年共同经历的悬念。

00:35:39.119 --> 00:35:44.599
But I'm curious if you also felt like this was some sort of turning point for the show.
不过我很好奇，你们是否也觉得这是该剧的一个转折点。

00:35:44.599 --> 00:35:48.119
if you felt like it was this episode that really hooked people.
你们是否觉得正是这一集真正吸引了观众？

00:35:48.119 --> 00:35:50.119
And if so, why?
如果是的话，为什么？

00:35:50.119 --> 00:35:51.320
That's a great question.
这真是个好问题。

00:35:51.320 --> 00:35:54.840
I love that she pointed out the Robin of it all because we haven't talked that much about that.
我很高兴她指出了“罗宾的特质”这一点，因为我们之前没怎么讨论过这个。

00:35:54.840 --> 00:36:02.119
It happens later in the episode, but the reveal that Robin went to the wedding and saw Ted and Victoria seemingly kissing.
这发生在剧集的后半部分，但那个揭晓是：罗宾去了婚礼现场，看到了泰德和维多利亚似乎在接吻。

00:36:02.119 --> 00:36:08.480
Of course, she didn't know they were gonna pull up at the last minute from actually kissing and then cried in the bathroom.
当然，她并不知道他们在最后一刻忍住没真的吻上去，然后她在洗手间里哭了。

00:36:08.480 --> 00:36:19.000
I totally, Jordana, that's a great point because seeing her in tears in that bathroom stall is a huge pivot point for the Robin and Ted of it all, and so many other things.
